Bundled fonts (plugins/fonts-default/fonts) are licensed under the SIL Open
Font License, Version 1.1:

- Literata, Copyright 2017 The Literata Project Authors
  (https://github.com/googlefonts/literata)
- Source Sans 3, Copyright 2010-2023 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/), with
  Reserved Font Name 'Source' (https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-sans),
  bundled unmodified as SourceSans3.ttf. The Xteink readers draw the
  interface from bitmap packs made from it (one weight, Latin letters
  only, rasterised): a Modified Version under the licence, so they are
  named PaperPaw Sans, not with the Reserved Font Name, and are licensed
  under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, as the font they are
  derived from.

The icon font (plugins/fonts-default/fonts/PaperPawIcons.ttf) is a subset of
Tabler Icons, Copyright 2020-2025 Paweł Kuna (https://tabler.io/icons),
licensed under the MIT License (fonts/TablerIcons-MIT.txt).

Hyphenation patterns (plugins/hyphenation/patterns, built in, and
plugins/hyphenation-de/patterns, a plugin of the store) come from the
hyph-utf8 project (https://github.com/hyphenation/tex-hyphen):

- German, reformed spelling, Copyright (c) 2013-2024 Stephan Hennig,
  Werner Lemberg, Günter Milde, Sander van Geloven, Georg Pfeiffer,
  Gisbert W. Selke, Tobias Wendorf, Keno Wehr, licensed under the MIT
  License.
- American English, Copyright (C) 1990, 2004, 2005 Gerard D.C. Kuiken,
  under an all-permissive license.

Their notices are in the patterns' README.md files.

The firmware of the Xteink readers also contains:

- Display initialisation sequences and waveform tables derived from the
  FreeInk SDK, Copyright (c) 2026 FreeInk, and the OpenX4 E-Paper
  Community SDK, Copyright (c) 2025 Open X4 E-Paper Contributors, both
  licensed under the MIT License (its text is below, with the crates').
- Battery gauge and board facts after Papyrix, Copyright (c) 2026 Pavel
  Liashkov, licensed under the MIT License.
- Mbed TLS (https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls), Copyright The Mbed TLS
  Contributors, used under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (one of its
  two licences).
- The Wi-Fi, Bluetooth LE and radio libraries of ESP-IDF
  (https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf), Copyright Espressif Systems
  (Shanghai) Co., Ltd., provided as binaries for Espressif's chips and
  licensed as ESP-IDF states (Apache License, Version 2.0), and ESP-IDF's
  second-stage bootloader, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
- Mozilla's list of certificate authorities (webpki-roots), under the
  Community Data License Agreement Permissive 2.0, whose text is below.

Patched copies of fatfs, trouble-host and jni-macros (patches/) keep their
licences; their changes are marked "Modified for PaperPaw".

The cats (the sleeping cat in plugins/sleep/pictures, the reading cats in
plugins/reading-goal/pictures, the README's pictures in docs/images/readme
and their dark versions) are PaperPaw artwork, generated with an AI
image model (Google Nano Banana) for the project, and licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, as the rest of PaperPaw.
